module nysd-local-rules.local-rules

import core.states.new-york.{ frcp6-new-york }

// The Southern District of New York's own periods under the Joint Local
// Rules, computed under the federal rules (Local Civ. R. 6.1(a), (b): "In
// computing periods of days, refer to Fed. R. Civ. P. 6"). The motion
// periods of Local Civ. R. 6.1 apply "unless provided otherwise by statute
// or rule, or by the court in a judge's individual practices or in a
// direction in a particular case". Rules that state no period or limit
// stay out: admission, appearances and discipline (Local Civ. R. 1.3-1.6),
// electronic filing (5.2), orders on motions (6.2), motions in limine
// (6.4), motion content and formatting (7.1(a), (b)), pro se authorities
// (7.2), scheduling-order exemptions (16.1, 16.2), privilege logs and
// discovery definitions (26.2-26.5), depositions (30.1-30.4), discovery
// disputes (37.1, 37.2), summations and trial scheduling (39.2, 40.1),
// default (55.1, 55.2), summary judgment statements (56.1, 56.2), consent
// to a magistrate judge (73.1), removal (81.1) and mediation (83.9).
// Periods the rules state in weeks stay in notes, because lit/core counts
// days, months and years: under the Local Civ. R. 83.10 plan, amendment to
// name additional defendants without leave within six weeks after the
// first defendant answers (83.10(f)), the plaintiff's settlement demand
// within six weeks after that answer and the defendant's written response
// within 14 days thereafter (83.10(g)), and the status letter within 10
// weeks after that answer (83.10(h)). The plan's answer periods measured
// from "the greater of" two dates stay in notes (83.10(c)): a defendant
// served after the first has the greater of 60 days or the first-served
// defendant's date, and a defendant served the release after the complaint
// has the greater of 60 days from service of the release or 60 days after
// its own service. The clerk's transfer of a case upon the expiration of
// seven days (Local Civ. R. 83.1) binds the clerk, not a party, and is
// not declared. Pro se page limits are stated in notes: briefs that are
// handwritten or typewritten by an unrepresented party may not exceed 25
// pages and replies 10 pages (Local Civ. R. 7.1(c); Local Soc. Sec. R.
// 5.1), or 10 and five pages on reconsideration (Local Civ. R. 6.3).
// Amounts in the rules are not declared. The Eastern District Only rules
// (court-annexed arbitration and mediation, 83.7 and 83.8) are lit/nyed's.
// The earlier S.D.N.Y. outline's FRCP flow and its Supreme Court decisions
// (Twombly, Iqbal, Celotex, Anderson v. Liberty Lobby) are FRCP authority
// and belong to lit/frcp; they are removed here: no reporter text is
// vendored.
/// A brief in support of or in response to a motion, filed by an attorney
/// or prepared with a computer: at most 8,750 words, excluding the caption,
/// index, tables, signature blocks and required certificates (Local Civ. R.
/// 7.1(c)).
limit motion-brief {
  words <= 8_750 cite "S.D.N.Y. Local Civ. R. 7.1(c)"
} cite "S.D.N.Y. Local Civ. R. 7.1(c)"

/// A reply brief on a motion, filed by an attorney or prepared with a
/// computer: at most 3,500 words (Local Civ. R. 7.1(c)).
limit reply-brief {
  words <= 3_500 cite "S.D.N.Y. Local Civ. R. 7.1(c)"
} cite "S.D.N.Y. Local Civ. R. 7.1(c)"

/// A brief in support of or in response to a motion for reconsideration,
/// filed by an attorney or prepared with a computer: at most 3,500 words
/// unless the court provides otherwise (Local Civ. R. 6.3).
limit reconsideration-brief {
  words <= 3_500 cite "S.D.N.Y. Local Civ. R. 6.3"
} cite "S.D.N.Y. Local Civ. R. 6.3"

/// A reply brief on a motion for reconsideration, filed by an attorney or
/// prepared with a computer: at most 1,750 words (Local Civ. R. 6.3).
limit reconsideration-reply-brief {
  words <= 1_750 cite "S.D.N.Y. Local Civ. R. 6.3"
} cite "S.D.N.Y. Local Civ. R. 6.3"

/// An initial or opposition brief in a Social Security action, filed by an
/// attorney or prepared with a computer: at most 8,750 words absent leave
/// requested at least seven days in advance (Local Soc. Sec. R. 5.1).
limit social-security-brief {
  words <= 8_750 cite "S.D.N.Y. Local Soc. Sec. R. 5.1"
} cite "S.D.N.Y. Local Soc. Sec. R. 5.1"

/// A plaintiff's reply brief in a Social Security action, filed by an
/// attorney or prepared with a computer: at most 3,500 words (Local Soc.
/// Sec. R. 5.1).
limit social-security-reply-brief {
  words <= 3_500 cite "S.D.N.Y. Local Soc. Sec. R. 5.1"
} cite "S.D.N.Y. Local Soc. Sec. R. 5.1"

/// Moving papers on a motion or application under FRCP 26 through 37 or
/// 45(d)(3) are served (Local Civ. R. 6.1(a)).
event DiscoveryMotionServed() paper motion-brief
/// Opposing or response papers on a discovery motion are served (Local
/// Civ. R. 6.1(a)).
event DiscoveryOppositionServed() paper motion-brief
/// Moving papers on any other civil motion, petition or application are
/// served (Local Civ. R. 6.1(b)).
event MotionServed() paper motion-brief
/// Opposing or response papers on any other motion are served (Local Civ.
/// R. 6.1(b)).
event OppositionServed() paper motion-brief
/// A reply is served (Local Civ. R. 6.1, 7.1(c)).
event ReplyServed() paper reply-brief
/// The court's order sought to be reconsidered is entered (Local Civ. R.
/// 6.3).
event OrderEntered()
/// A notice of motion for reconsideration and its memorandum are served
/// (Local Civ. R. 6.3).
event ReconsiderationMotionServed() paper reconsideration-brief
/// A reply memorandum on reconsideration is served (Local Civ. R. 6.3).
event ReconsiderationReplyServed() paper reconsideration-reply-brief
/// The information required in a disclosure statement changes (Local Civ.
/// R. 7.1.1).
event DisclosureInformationChanged()
/// The court rules that a motion to dismiss or for judgment on the
/// pleadings against a pro se party will be treated as one for summary
/// judgment (Local Civ. R. 12.1).
event ConversionRuled()
/// The court grants a motion to amend or supplement a pleading under FRCP
/// 15(a)(2) or (d) (Local Civ. R. 15.1(b)).
event AmendmentGranted()
/// The complaint in a prisoner pro se action is served on a named
/// defendant (Local Civ. R. 33.2(d)).
event PrisonerComplaintServed()
/// The discovery cut-off date (Local Civ. R. 33.3(c)).
event DiscoveryCutoff()
/// A final decision is rendered and no appeal is taken (Local Civ. R.
/// 39.1(b)(1)).
event FinalDecisionRendered()
/// The appeal is finally disposed of (Local Civ. R. 39.1(b)(2), 54.1(a)).
event AppealDisposed()
/// Final judgment is entered (Local Civ. R. 54.1(a)).
event FinalJudgmentEntered()
/// An objection to a magistrate judge's order on a nondispositive matter
/// is served (Local Civ. R. 72.1(b)(1)).
event MagistrateObjectionServed()
/// The plaintiff's brief in a Social Security action is due under
/// Supplemental Social Security Rule 6 (Local Soc. Sec. R. 7.1).
event PlaintiffBriefDue()
/// The Commissioner's brief is served on a pro se plaintiff (Local Soc.
/// Sec. R. 8.1).
event CommissionerBriefServed() paper social-security-brief
/// In a Local Civ. R. 83.10 case, the complaint is first served together
/// with the release for sealed arrest records (Local Civ. R. 83.10(c)).
event PlanComplaintServedWithRelease()
/// In a Local Civ. R. 83.10 case, the first defendant files an answer
/// (Local Civ. R. 83.10(d)-(h)).
event PlanFirstAnswerFiled()

/// Local Civ. R. 6.1(a): on a motion or application under FRCP 26 through
/// 37 and 45(d)(3), opposing or response papers are served within seven
/// days after service of the moving papers.
deadline discovery-opposition-period: 7.days after DiscoveryMotionServed() counted_by frcp6-new-york cite "S.D.N.Y. Local Civ. R. 6.1(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// Local Civ. R. 6.1(a): reply papers on such a motion are served within
/// two days after service of the answering papers.
deadline discovery-reply-period: 2.days after DiscoveryOppositionServed() counted_by frcp6-new-york cite "S.D.N.Y. Local Civ. R. 6.1(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// Local Civ. R. 6.1(b): on any other civil motion, petition or
/// application (other than a habeas corpus petition), opposing or response
/// papers are served within 14 days after service of the moving papers.
deadline opposition-period: 14.days after MotionServed() counted_by frcp6-new-york cite "S.D.N.Y. Local Civ. R. 6.1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// Local Civ. R. 6.1(b): reply papers are served within seven days after
/// service of the answering papers.
deadline reply-period: 7.days after OppositionServed() counted_by frcp6-new-york cite "S.D.N.Y. Local Civ. R. 6.1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// Local Civ. R. 6.3: unless the court, a statute or a rule (such as FRCP
/// 50, 52 and 59) provides otherwise, a notice of motion for
/// reconsideration is served within 14 days after the entry of the order
/// challenged; answering and reply memoranda follow Local Civ. R. 6.1(a)
/// or (b).
deadline reconsideration-period: 14.days after OrderEntered() counted_by frcp6-new-york cite "S.D.N.Y. Local Civ. R. 6.3"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// Local Civ. R. 7.1.1: for FRCP 7.1(b)(2), "promptly" means within 14
/// days; a supplemental disclosure statement is filed within 14 days of
/// any change in the required information.
deadline supplemental-disclosure-period: 14.days after DisclosureInformationChanged() counted_by frcp6-new-york cite "S.D.N.Y. Local Civ. R. 7.1.1"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// Local Civ. R. 12.1: when the court treats a motion against a pro se
/// party as one for summary judgment and the movant has not served the
/// required notice, the movant serves and files the amended notice within
/// 14 days of the ruling.
deadline pro-se-notice-period: 14.days after ConversionRuled() counted_by frcp6-new-york cite "S.D.N.Y. Local Civ. R. 12.1"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// Local Civ. R. 15.1(b): unless the court orders otherwise, a represented
/// moving party files the amended or supplemental pleading within seven
/// days of the order granting the motion.
deadline amended-pleading-period: 7.days after AmendmentGranted() counted_by frcp6-new-york cite "S.D.N.Y. Local Civ. R. 15.1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// Local Civ. R. 33.2(d): the standard prisoner pro se interrogatories and
/// requests for production are answered within 120 days of service of the
/// complaint on any named defendant, unless the court orders otherwise for
/// good cause or a dispositive motion is pending.
deadline prisoner-discovery-period: 120.days after PrisonerComplaintServed() counted_by frcp6-new-york cite "S.D.N.Y. Local Civ. R. 33.2(d)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// Local Civ. R. 33.3(c) (Southern District only): unless the court has
/// ordered otherwise, contention interrogatories may be served at the
/// conclusion of other discovery and at least 30 days before the discovery
/// cut-off date.
deadline contention-interrogatory-period: 30.days before DiscoveryCutoff() counted_by frcp6-new-york cite "S.D.N.Y. Local Civ. R. 33.3(c)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// Local Civ. R. 39.1(b)(1): filed trial and hearing exhibits are removed
/// within 90 days after a final decision is rendered, if no appeal is
/// taken.
deadline exhibit-removal-period: 90.days after FinalDecisionRendered() counted_by frcp6-new-york cite "S.D.N.Y. Local Civ. R. 39.1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// Local Civ. R. 39.1(b)(2): if an appeal has been taken, filed exhibits
/// are removed within 30 days after the final disposition of the appeal.
deadline exhibit-removal-appeal-period: 30.days after AppealDisposed() counted_by frcp6-new-york cite "S.D.N.Y. Local Civ. R. 39.1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// Local Civ. R. 54.1(a): unless the court extends the period for good
/// cause, a party seeking costs files a notice of taxation of costs within
/// 30 days after the entry of final judgment; a party that does not is
/// deemed to have waived costs.
deadline taxation-notice-period: 30.days after FinalJudgmentEntered() counted_by frcp6-new-york cite "S.D.N.Y. Local Civ. R. 54.1(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// Local Civ. R. 54.1(a): in the case of an appeal by any party, the
/// notice of taxation of costs is filed within 30 days after the final
/// disposition of the appeal.
deadline taxation-notice-appeal-period: 30.days after AppealDisposed() counted_by frcp6-new-york cite "S.D.N.Y. Local Civ. R. 54.1(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// Local Civ. R. 72.1(b)(1): a response to an objection to a magistrate
/// judge's order on a nondispositive matter is served within 14 days after
/// being served with the objection.
deadline magistrate-objection-response-period: 14.days after MagistrateObjectionServed() counted_by frcp6-new-york cite "S.D.N.Y. Local Civ. R. 72.1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// Local Soc. Sec. R. 7.1: if a pro se plaintiff files no brief within the
/// time set by Supplemental Social Security Rule 6, the Commissioner files
/// and serves a brief within 30 days after the plaintiff's brief was due.
deadline commissioner-pro-se-brief-period: 30.days after PlaintiffBriefDue() counted_by frcp6-new-york cite "S.D.N.Y. Local Soc. Sec. R. 7.1"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// Local Soc. Sec. R. 8.1: the pro se plaintiff's brief in opposition is
/// filed and served within 14 days after service of the Commissioner's
/// brief.
deadline pro-se-opposition-period: 14.days after CommissionerBriefServed() counted_by frcp6-new-york cite "S.D.N.Y. Local Soc. Sec. R. 8.1"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// Local Civ. R. 83.10(c) (Southern District only): if the release for
/// sealed arrest records is served when the complaint is first served, the
/// defendant has 80 days from that service to answer; a motion to dismiss
/// the entire complaint stays the plan's deadlines unless the court orders
/// otherwise.
deadline plan-answer-period: 80.days after PlanComplaintServedWithRelease() counted_by frcp6-new-york cite "S.D.N.Y. Local Civ. R. 83.10(c)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// Local Civ. R. 83.10(d)(1): within 14 days after the first defendant
/// answers, the parties confer under FRCP 26(f).
deadline plan-conference-period: 14.days after PlanFirstAnswerFiled() counted_by frcp6-new-york cite "S.D.N.Y. Local Civ. R. 83.10(d)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// Local Civ. R. 83.10(d)(1): an application to exempt the case from the
/// plan is submitted no later than 21 days after the first defendant
/// answers.
deadline plan-exemption-period: 21.days after PlanFirstAnswerFiled() counted_by frcp6-new-york cite "S.D.N.Y. Local Civ. R. 83.10(d)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// Local Civ. R. 83.10(d)(2): within 21 days after the first defendant
/// answers, the parties exchange initial disclosures.
deadline plan-disclosure-period: 21.days after PlanFirstAnswerFiled() counted_by frcp6-new-york cite "S.D.N.Y. Local Civ. R. 83.10(d)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// Local Civ. R. 83.10(e): within 28 days after the first defendant
/// answers, the parties complete production of the plan's limited
/// discovery.
deadline plan-discovery-period: 28.days after PlanFirstAnswerFiled() counted_by frcp6-new-york cite "S.D.N.Y. Local Civ. R. 83.10(e)"
{
  forum frcp
}

test "discovery opposition period: 7 days after the trigger" cite "S.D.N.Y. Local Civ. R. 6.1(a)"
{
  given DiscoveryMotionServed() on 2026-11-02
  expect deadline(discovery-opposition-period) == 2026-11-09
}

test "discovery reply period: 2 days after the trigger" cite "S.D.N.Y. Local Civ. R. 6.1(a)"
{
  given DiscoveryOppositionServed() on 2026-11-02
  expect deadline(discovery-reply-period) == 2026-11-04
}

test "opposition period: 14 days after the trigger" cite "S.D.N.Y. Local Civ. R. 6.1(b)"
{
  given MotionServed() on 2026-11-02
  expect deadline(opposition-period) == 2026-11-16
}

test "reply period: 7 days after the trigger" cite "S.D.N.Y. Local Civ. R. 6.1(b)"
{
  given OppositionServed() on 2026-11-02
  expect deadline(reply-period) == 2026-11-09
}

